#: src/ui/ui_common.cpp
msgid "The Hikaru draws 640x480 pictures (854x480 in widescreen). Black bars: the whole picture in its shape, with black bars where the screen's shape differs. Whole multiples: the same, at 1x, 2x, 3x... the native size only, for sharp pixels. Stretched: the picture fills the window, deformed."
msgstr ""

#: src/ui/ui_common.cpp
msgid "Vertical sync"
msgstr ""

#: src/ui/ui_common.cpp
msgid "Limit the frame rate"
msgstr ""

#: src/ui/ui_common.cpp
msgid "Target frame rate"
msgstr ""

#: src/ui/ui_common.cpp
msgid "Show the frame rate (F12)"
msgstr ""

#: src/ui/ui_common.cpp
msgid "Show the frame number in the title bar"
msgstr ""

#: src/ui/ui_common.cpp
msgid "Hide the mouse pointer"
msgstr ""

#: src/ui/ui_common.cpp
msgid "Draw on a thread of its own"
msgstr ""

#: src/ui/ui_common.cpp
msgid "Each frame drawn while the next one is emulated: faster when the drawing slows the game, but the picture comes a frame later. Takes effect at the game's next start."
msgstr ""

#: src/ui/ui_common.cpp
msgid "Its resolution's (square pixels)"
msgstr ""

#: src/ui/ui_common.cpp
msgid "Screen shape"
msgstr ""

#: src/ui/ui_common.cpp
msgid "The picture is placed by the screen's shape: that of its resolution, or 4:3 or 16:9 whatever its resolution, for a CRT's super resolutions (1920x240): the black bars right, and stretched from 4:3 to 16:9 no more."
msgstr ""

#: src/ui/ui_common.cpp
msgid "Sharp"
msgstr ""

#: src/ui/ui_common.cpp
msgid "Smooth"
msgstr ""

#: src/ui/ui_common.cpp
msgid "Scaling filter"
msgstr ""

#: src/ui/ui_common.cpp
msgid "Smooth: down to 240 rows (a CRT), each one the mean of two, where Sharp drops one in two (thin lines, small texts)."
msgstr ""

#: src/ui/ui_common.cpp
msgid "Widescreen 3D (16:9)"
msgstr ""

#: src/ui/ui_common.cpp
msgid "4:3, in the middle"
msgstr ""

#: src/ui/ui_common.cpp
msgid "Stretched to 16:9"
msgstr ""

#: src/ui/ui_common.cpp
msgid "2D in widescreen"
msgstr ""

#: src/ui/ui_common.cpp
msgid "The 3D seen wider, at 16:9, its middle as the game draws it; the 2D (texts, logos) at 4:3 in the middle, or stretched for a game that needs it. The game may leave objects out at the sides, made for 4:3. Takes effect at the game's next start."
msgstr ""

#: src/ui/ui_common.cpp
msgid "Draw distance"
msgstr ""

#: src/ui/ui_common.cpp
msgid "The 3D scenery's detailed models and its fog that much farther; what the game itself leaves out is not drawn. x1.0: as the game draws it."
msgstr ""

#: src/ui/ui_common.cpp
msgid "The sound card's own"
msgstr ""

#: src/ui/ui_common.cpp
msgid "Mono"
msgstr ""

#: src/ui/ui_common.cpp
msgid "Stereo"
msgstr ""

#: src/ui/ui_common.cpp
msgid "2.1 (stereo and subwoofer)"
msgstr ""

#: src/ui/ui_common.cpp
msgid "Quad (front and rear)"
msgstr ""

#: src/ui/ui_common.cpp
msgid "Speakers"
msgstr ""

#: src/ui/ui_common.cpp
msgid "The game's sound is its cabinet's: the front speakers', and the rear's when it has some. The rear goes to the rear speakers (quad, 5.1, 7.1), or into the front without; the subwoofer gets all of the sound, low-passed; the center speaker none. The sound card's own: the speakers Windows has set for it."
msgstr ""

#: src/ui/ui_common.cpp
msgid "Front / rear balance"
msgstr ""

#: src/ui/ui_common.cpp
msgid "Front at %d %%, rear at %d %%; 50 for both at their full level."
msgstr ""

#: src/ui/ui_common.cpp
msgid "Volume"
msgstr ""

#: src/ui/ui_common.cpp
msgid "The changes take effect as soon as the game goes on."
msgstr ""

#: src/ui/ui_common.cpp
msgid "The board's setting"
msgstr ""

#: src/ui/ui_common.cpp
msgid "Off"
msgstr ""

#: src/ui/ui_common.cpp
msgid "On"
msgstr ""

#: src/ui/ui_common.cpp
msgid "Attract sound"
msgstr ""

#: src/ui/ui_common.cpp
msgid "The sound of the game's attract, while nobody plays. Written to the game's EEPROM at its start; the board's setting: as its BIOS menu set it (ADVERTISE SOUND, off on a new board)."
msgstr ""

#: src/ui/ui_common.cpp
msgid "Latency"
msgstr ""

#: src/ui/ui_common.cpp
msgid "The sound kept ahead in the output: less, the sound closer to the picture, but gaps when a frame comes late; more, safer on a slow PC. The output opens again with it."
msgstr ""

#: src/ui/ui_common.cpp
msgid "Optimized"
msgstr ""

#: src/ui/ui_common.cpp
msgid "Interpreted"
msgstr ""

#: src/ui/ui_common.cpp
msgid "Sound emulation"
msgstr ""

#: src/ui/ui_common.cpp
msgid "Optimized keeps the sound chips' channel registers and effects program decoded until the game writes them; interpreted decodes them at each sample, slower, as the reference. The same sound either way; the change takes effect at once."
msgstr ""

#: src/ui/ui_common.cpp
msgid "Fake the MIE (Valkyrie's hack)"
msgstr ""

#: src/ui/ui_common.cpp
msgid "Off, the MIE's Z80 runs the game's program and drives the JVS bus, where the I/O board has the controls. On, Valkyrie's hack fakes its answers, with the Test and Service switches alone. The MIE_HACK environment variable, when set, wins over this setting."
msgstr ""

#: src/ui/ui_common.cpp
msgid "The board's own"
msgstr ""

#: src/ui/ui_common.cpp
msgid "Japan"
msgstr ""

#: src/ui/ui_common.cpp
msgid "USA"
msgstr ""

#: src/ui/ui_common.cpp
msgid "Export"
msgstr ""

#: src/ui/ui_common.cpp
msgid "Australia"
msgstr ""

#: src/ui/ui_common.cpp
msgid "Korea"
msgstr ""

#: src/ui/ui_common.cpp
msgid "Region"
msgstr ""

#: src/ui/ui_common.cpp
msgid "The board's country, which the games read for their language and texts (Brave Firefighters in English outside Japan). Written to the game's EEPROM at its start; the board's own: the country its BIOS menu set."
msgstr ""

#: src/ui/ui_common.cpp
msgid "Dynamic recompiler (dynarec)"
msgstr ""

#: src/ui/ui_common.cpp
msgid "Interpreter"
msgstr ""

#: src/ui/ui_common.cpp
msgid "SH-4 processors"
msgstr ""

#: src/ui/ui_common.cpp
msgid "The dynarec runs their code translated to x86-64; the interpreter, one instruction at a time, as the debugger does. Both give the same machine: the change takes effect at the next frame."
msgstr ""

#: src/ui/ui_common.cpp
msgid "Regions, one after the other"
msgstr ""

#: src/ui/ui_common.cpp
msgid "Page table"
msgstr ""

#: src/ui/ui_common.cpp
msgid "Fastmem"
msgstr ""

#: src/ui/ui_common.cpp
msgid "Fastmem takes much more memory: 512 MB of address space reserved for each SH-4, their RAM and ROM mapped there a second time. For no significant gain in emulation speed."
msgstr ""

#: src/ui/ui_common.cpp
msgid "Memory access"
msgstr ""

#: src/ui/ui_common.cpp
msgid "How the CPUs find their RAM and ROM: the page table at once, the regions searched one after the other (the first way), fastmem at their own addresses in the PC's address space. The same machine either way: the change takes effect at the next frame."
msgstr ""

#: src/ui/ui_common.cpp
msgid "SH-4 clock"
msgstr ""

#: src/ui/ui_common.cpp
msgid "The SH-4s' clock: 200 MHz is the board's. Their timers, the MIE and the sound keep real time at any clock; the faster, the more of the PC the waits the games poll take (at 200 MHz, the games' boots run below 60 frames a second on this PC). 57 MHz by default."
msgstr ""

